In a resolution of the Supreme Court dated September 22, 1994, it was reiterated that the temporary restraining order (TRO) issued on June 30, 1994 has not been lifted. Accordingly, all registration and collection processes towards the effective implementation of Republic Act 7716 are hereby postponed indefinitely until further orders from this office. cda

In the meantime, you are hereby directed to continue with our VAT educational and information campaign as well as the strategic action plan of:

1. Identifying weak and strong points on the VAT collections from existing VAT and Non-VAT taxpayers (e.g. identify all taxpayers from whom substantial VAT revenues may be collected; areas for leakages on VAT revenues, and etc.);

2. Further increasing the tax base by undertaking continuous and intensified tax mapping operations;

3. Maximizing collection of expanded withholding taxes;

4. Intensifying third party information gathering for tax assessment purposes;

5. Continuing with the registration of VAT and Non-VAT taxpayers pursuant to the provisions of the old VAT Law (EO 273) for NEW taxpayers; and cda

6. Identifying specific areas or industries where VAT collection dropped by updating the masterlist of VAT taxpayers. cd

Strict compliance is hereby enjoined.

LIWAYWAY VINZONS-CHATO
Commissioner of Internal Revenue

In line with the program of this Bureau to intensify VAT information and educational campaign, and in order not to disrupt the on-going work schedule and plan of activities of our field offices, the effectivity of Revenue Travel Assignment Order (RTAO) Nos. 73-94, 74-94, 75-94, 76-94 are hereby deferred and shall take effect on October 1, 1994. Thus, all Revenue Officers affected by said RTAO's shall have a synchronized reporting for duty to their respective new assignments on October 1, 1994.

In this regard, to ensure an orderly turn-over of inventories of pending cases with the Revenue Officers who are being transferred out of their respective Revenue District Office the following procedures must first be complied with: cd

1. Immediate turnover of inventories of pending cases as of 07-30-94 that have been assigned to them 1 to 6 months before September 30, 1994;

2. All cases pending over 6 months must be terminated with the corresponding report of investigation and to be transmitted to the Assessment Division on or before September 30, 1994;

3. The Regional Offices must only issue the required Certificate of Clearance to the concerned Revenue Officer only upon his full compliance with the above procedures;

4. Upon full compliance with the above requirements, Revenue Officers affected by RTAO Nos. 73-94 to 76-94 must report to their new assignments not later than October 1, 1994;

5. No Letter of Authority should be issued to any Revenue Officer unless he presents a Regional Clearance from his previous assignment. 

Any violation hereof shall be considered as a grave offense subject to administrative charge and/or expulsion from the revenue service under the provisions of the Civil Service Law and Rules.

For strict compliance.

LIWAYWAY VINZONS-CHATO
Commissioner

