I. OBJECTIVES :

In line with the implementation of the National Tax Consciousness Year and the sustained taxpayer information and assistance campaign, pursuant to RMO 7-94, all revenue district offices are required to establish a Taxpayers' Service Counter within their office premises that would serve the following objectives:

1. project a service-oriented image of the BIR;

2. promote the delivery of fast, efficient and courteous "frontline" service to the taxpayers; 

3. provide a place that would serve as a reception area for taxpayers;

4. serve as a "one-stop shop" to address the taxpayers' needs without the need for them to follow up with or be referred to other offices; and

5. administer the taxpayer perception survey to assist in the evaluation of the effectiveness of the taxpayer service rendered

II. GUIDELINES :

1. The Taxpayers' Service Counter should be set up in a conspicuous place preferable near the entrance of the district office;

2. The counter should be open for service from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM with no noon breaks;

3. A sign identifying the counter and flowcharts of frontline service procedures as prescribed in RMO 47-93 should be displayed prominently near the counter;

4. Chairs, tables and a telephone should be provided for the exclusive use of the counter and/or taxpayers;

5. Information materials such as Philippine Revenue Journals, leaflets, primers, revenue issuances and other documents should be available for the taxpayers' perusal. acd

6. A tax form counter should be provided to carry all tax forms/returns.

7. Competent revenue personnel, preferably from the Taxpayer Assistance Unit, should be assigned by the Revenue District Officer to the counter to handle queries or to assist taxpayers of their requirements;

8. A logbook containing the taxpayer name, address, telephone number, the nature and date of query or service required, the nature and date of information of action taken, and the name of the revenue personnel, should be maintained to record the activities of the Taxpayers' Service Counter.

9. The revenue personnel in the counter should distribute the Taxpayer Perception Survey Slip (Annex A) to all taxpayers to whom service has been rendered and advice them to accomplish and drop the said slips in the drop box;

10. A drop box should be posted where the Taxpayer Perception Survey Slips can be placed;

11. A report containing the results of the taxpayer service counter activities and taxpayer perception survey (Annex B) should be prepared monthly and filed, together with the survey slips, for reference of the Revenue District Officer and for evaluation of the National Office Audit Team that will visit the district offices.

III. FEEDBACK MECHANISM :

All revenue district officers must submit a report and pictures of the establishment of Taxpayers' Service Counter to the Management & Planning Service, copy furnished the Regional Directors, not later than February 28, 1994. cda

IV. REPEALING CLAUSE:

This Order repeals Revenue Memorandum Order No. 10-88 which creates the "Express Lane" Assistance Counter.

LIWAYWAY VINZONS-CHATO
Commissioner of Internal Revenue

