5. 100% of the specific tax on denatured alcohol used for motive power;

6. 100% of the 2% tax on sugar controls under Sec. 189 of the National Internal Revenue Code;

7. 10% of the ad valorem and royalties on mines;

8. 100% of the tobacco inspection fees;

9. 100% of the national park fund; and

10. internal revenue taxes and fees that accrue directly to the local governments.

In reporting the collections made by regional offices the particular taxes where there are exclusions for special fund purposes should be detailed by showing therein the gross amount of collections, the percentage accruing to the special fund and the net amount accruing to the general fund. The net amount should be the only amount that is to be taken into account and included in the other general fund collections in determining the overall accomplishments of the region or the inspection district as the case may be. cdt

